From 3a3094e994a994dbe3eaa829469b851fb9949fb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:28:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 064/116] bit_write_UMC: the shortest form

Only the first 4 of the 8 groups were checked for leading zeros, so every
value took at least 4 bytes: handle offset 1 in the object map was
81 80 80 00, AutoCAD writes 01. Readers accept it, but the object map
grew by a third (2004/Line.dwg: 1174 bytes, AutoCAD 674).

* src/bits.c (bit_write_UMC): Drop all zero high groups, keep the extra
byte for 0x40 as before (as AutoCAD: e8 00).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/bits.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/bits.c b/src/bits.c
index bc506a2..7e7745a 100644
--- a/src/bits.c
+++ b/src/bits.c
@@ -1116,7 +1116,8 @@ bit_write_UMC (Bit_Chain *dat, BITCODE_UMC val)
       byte[i] |= 0x80;
       mask = mask << 7;
     }
-  for (i = 0; i < 4; i++)
+  // the shortest form, the high zero groups dropped
+  for (i = 0; i < MAX_BYTE_UMC - 1; i++)
     if (byte[i] & 0x7f)
       break;
 
